From d2676989ebde539af3f4fcea6eeac3a01b29b951 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:19:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/65] Restart the C port from the assembly, routine by
 routine

Remove the old readable layer and start a new port in src_c/readable,
written by hand from rebuild/source:

- H000 entry with the original 99 module initialisations, H001 main,
  H002 DOS adapters, H003 memory adapters, H015 runtime start/exit and
  32-bit arithmetic (15/902 routines).
- Routines not yet ported stop the program with their address
  (unported.c), so the port runs exactly as far as it is ported.
- scripts/port_status.py generates PORT_STATUS.md from the ROUTINE
  sheets of the asm and the PORT markers in the sources.
- The Ghidra reference build keeps its runtime support files, moved to
  src_c/reference_runtime.
- .gitignore no longer ignores directories named "cok"; runtime_test
  uses an A5 frame pointer inside its buffer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013G8KST8dgGfenpqx3RukYi
